ugh.  The way that I pronounced "r" in that audio had absolutely ZERO "e" in
it (at least to my ears).  Arbitrarily dropping vowels in
word pronunciation just feels so friggin' unlojbanic that I'm a little
offput right now.

Ok, if my "er" are both your "eir" and your "er" does that mean that you
can't hear a difference?  If that's the case then I'm going to just keep
pronouncing "er" like I have been and should I need to say "eir" I'll do it
the same way that I do it in the audio.  It's up to you to develop the ear
to hear the difference.  If enough people say "nope, I can't hear the
difference either" I'll conceded and just start dropping vowels when doing
otherwise confuses people.

